    <section>
      <p class="wide">
        Configure Simple Java Mail through its <strong>Java API</strong>, <strong>system properties</strong>, <strong>environment variables</strong>, or
        <strong>property files</strong>. The <a href="/spring.html">Spring integration</a> reads the same settings from Spring's environment.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="introduction">
    <div class="wide">
      <p>
Simple Java Mail combines loaded settings with choices made in Java. Java Mailer choices override ordinary loaded defaults;
conflicting explicit connection settings are rejected unless you select an override policy. Email defaults and overrides have separate field rules.
Mailer settings take effect at <code>buildMailer()</code>. Email templates take effect when you complete an Email or prepare it for sending.
See <a href="/understanding-configuration.html">Understanding configuration</a> for precedence, combined values and troubleshooting.
</p>
    </div>
    </section>

